# unit-watch.vrs: unit-watch D23's negative side and D34's first-move diagnostic (Session 1). A2 and A3: a unit is stuck by
# standing or still only while it holds a player as its aggro target, and NPCs drop even a forced target (`.devaggro`) on
# the invulnerable Chaos at once, so the positive standing and still cases wait for the owner's test weekend (D23, D34).
# What vrclient shows here: idle units beside a player are never marked, by any rule, the off-ground read included.
# Part 1: uw-wave (tools/vrclient/fixtures/uw-wave.json: a waveList SpawnWaves, wave 1 of 4 CHAR_Spider_Forest, wave 2 of 2
# waiting for its clear with no afterSeconds, 900 s, scoreboard on) at the mark uw-a (the pond) with Chaos there: for
# StuckSeconds + 30 s (120 s at the default 90) no "[nyar] unit-watch uw-wave stuck:" line of any reason; `.devaggroread`
# logs whether a forced target held (diagnostic only; Session 1: held=0 every time).
# Part 2 (diagnostic): uw-timing-a (12 then 6 CHAR_Spider_Forest) at uw-a with Chaos there and `.devaggro` on every spider;
# for 150 s the log collects one `[nyar watch] first-move event=uw-timing-a prefab=… after=<s> player=<target|none>` line
# per spider (after=none past 120 s unmoved) and no "(still)" mark. The measured default waits for the test weekend.
#
# Needs: a Release DLL with unit-watch step 3 and A2; NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devmark, .devgo, .devaggro, .devaggroread) and
# DevChatEcho; the dev events.json entries uw-wave and uw-timing-a (tools/vrclient/fixtures/uw-timing-a.json) enabled,
# every other spawning definition disabled; [Debug] VerboseLogging = true (part 2's lines); [Limits] MaxUnitsPerWave 12 or
# more; [UnitWatch] Enabled = true, StuckSeconds 90, StallMinutes 10 and SpawnStillSeconds 10 (the defaults: a 1-minute
# backstop would mark the spiders); [Scoreboard] IncludeAdmins = true; Chaos invulnerable (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a
# Boolean, never false).
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640 (uw-a: the pond, ground y about 0)
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=-?[0-9.]+ y=-?[0-9.]+ z=-?[0-9.]+
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devmark uw-a
expect-log \[DEV MARK\] uw-a
chat .nyar event set uw-wave location here
expect-reply uw-wave action.location =
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave started by manual timeout=20
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 10
chat .devaggro -581295882 30 4
expect-log \[DEV AGGRO\] put=(?P<AGG1>[0-9]+) held=
wait 5
chat .devaggroread -581295882 30
expect-log \[DEV AGGRO READ\] n=(?P<N1>[0-9]+) held=(?P<HELD1>[0-9]+)
chat .nyar debug here 30
expect-reply uw-wave
shot full uw-idle
# no mark of any reason on idle units beside Chaos (standing, still, off-ground)
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave stuck: timeout=120
chat .nyar event info uw-wave
expect-reply unit watch: 0 stuck now, 0 recovered, 0 removed
chat .nyar event stop uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
# part 2: first-move diagnostic, 12 spiders spawned beside Chaos at uw-a
chat .devgo uw-a
expect-log \[DEV TP\] uw-a
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar event set uw-timing-a location here
expect-reply uw-timing-a action.location =
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-timing-a
expect-log event uw-timing-a wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .devaggro -581295882 40 12
expect-log \[DEV AGGRO\] put=(?P<AGG>[0-9]+) held=
wait 5
chat .devaggroread -581295882 40
expect-log \[DEV AGGRO READ\] n=[0-9]+ held=(?P<HELD4>[0-9]+)
expect-log \[nyar watch\] first-move event=uw-timing-a prefab=CHAR_Spider_Forest after=([0-9.]+|none) player=(target|none) timeout=130
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-timing-a stuck: timeout=20
shot full uw-first-move
chat .nyar event stop uw-timing-a
expect-log event uw-timing-a stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
console TPHome
wait 3
